\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a connected reductive group over a global field, describe the constituents and multiplicities of the discrete automorphic spectrum by global Arthur parameters. The desired description must agree with the local parameterizations at each place and with the associated automorphic $L$-functions.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://www.claymath.org/library/monographs/cmim04c.pdf}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a connected reductive group over a global field, describe the constituents and multiplicities of the discrete automorphic spectrum by global Arthur parameters. The desired description must agree with the local parameterizations at each place and with the associated automorphic $L$-functions.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 1198 (ALG-034). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
